   "text": "{\"class\": \"one_plus_related\",\n \"explanation\": \"Responds to frontal faces of furry mammals, mainly cats, foxes, red pandas and other small carnivores and rodents, driven by the eye–nose region set in fur. It also fires weakly on face-like objects such as the front grille and headlight of a car.\",\n \"evidence\": \"All but one of the top 20 are frontal furry-animal faces. Occluding the face drops cat #2 from 9 to 1.1 and fox #1 from 10 to 2.4, while keeping only the face retains 40–56% (eyes alone or nose alone gives about 3.8–3.9); the car's activation sits on the grille/headlight side (4.5) and not the background (0.4).\",\n \"missing_data\": \"Human faces and non-furry animal faces (birds, reptiles), plus more face-like objects, to tell whether the unit is specific to mammal faces or responds to generic face configurations.\",\n \"confidence\": 0.7}",
